 105: **Finale composition (Opus B2 resolved):** build the shaft study in its own inspection-local **assembled solid pose**, independent of blueprint/exploded entry and current narrative explosion. Register revised parts and all selected legacy neighbour clones in that same assembled root before reveal. Prefer inspection-owned clones/named bundle; if narrative objects are reused, lease their complete parent/local transforms, visibility and materials, temporarily pose them to the inspection assembled frame, then restore them exactly on exit. Never reveal revised assembled supports among frozen exploded cages. The ring keeps its existing saved-composition behavior.
